<!-- keep-the-why:children -->
- unicorn-binance-websocket-api: https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/unicorn-binance-websocket-api — WebSocket stream client: stream setup and management, the receive loop, reconnects, websocket libraries (websockets/picows) and proxies, userData/listenKey streams incl. Portfolio Margin
- unicorn-binance-rest-api: https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/unicorn-binance-rest-api — REST client: endpoint coverage per Binance exchange (spot, margin, futures, options, Portfolio Margin, us, tr), request handling, listenKey endpoints, its CI test setup
- unicorn-binance-local-depth-cache: https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/unicorn-binance-local-depth-cache — local order books (DepthCaches): snapshot/stream sync and resync per exchange (spot, futures, options, margin), orphaned-level handling, the Python client for UBDCC
- unicorn-binance-depth-cache-cluster: https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/unicorn-binance-depth-cache-cluster — the DepthCache cluster (UBDCC): node roles, replication and failover, its REST API and error codes (fail-loud #6000), local and Kubernetes/Helm deployment, container images
- unicorn-binance-trailing-stop-loss: https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/unicorn-binance-trailing-stop-loss — trailing stop loss and smart entry engine and its CLI: stop-loss modes (incl. jump-in-and-trail), order placement and retry handling, CLI configuration
- unicorn-fy: https://github.com/oliver-zehentleitner/unicorn-fy — normalizing raw Binance payloads into consistent Python dicts: per-stream adapters, the userData envelope, event-type handling, JSON parsing (orjson)
<!-- /keep-the-why:children -->
